# ##########################
# 
# Template to control a group of vacuum components in sequence.
# (e.g. open|close valve, shutter, absorber sequentially)
# Developed to enable the automation of valve openings after sample change o I21.
# Generic database designed to work with any vacuum components.
# If a fast valve is used, an 'arm' delay must be set because there is no callback for this state in dlsPLC,
# and a pause is required once the 'open disarmed' state is reached before the 'arm' command can take effect
# (from testing, 30 sec. delay is recommended).
# Each vacumm element status is periodically monitored, and sequence steps are disabled accordingly.
# Currently, the open sequence doesn't include the fifth vacuum element.
# 
# Gregory Gay   01 July 2023
# 
# ###############################################
# 
# Macros:
# % macro, name, Object and gui association name
# % macro, P, EPICS name prefix
# % macro, R, EPICS name suffix
# % macro, VACNAME1, short name used to identify the first vacuum element
# % macro, DEVICE1, PV for the first element in the sequence
# % macro, DELAY1, ARM delay in seconds after the 'open disarmed' state (required for a fast valve, 30s recommended)
# % macro, VACNAME2, short name used to identify the second vacuum element
# % macro, DEVICE2, PV for the second element in the sequence
# % macro, DELAY2, ARM delay in seconds after the 'open disarmed' state (required for a fast valve, 30s recommended)
# % macro, VACNAME3, short name used to identify the third vacuum element
# % macro, DEVICE3, PV for the third element in the sequence
# % macro, DELAY3, ARM delay in seconds after the 'open disarmed' state (required for a fast valve, 30s recommended)
# % macro, VACNAME4, short name used to identify the fourth vacuum element
# % macro, DEVICE4, PV for the fourth element in the sequence
# % macro, DELAY4, ARM delay in seconds after the 'open disarmed' state (required for a fast valve, 30s recommended)
# % macro, VACNAME5, short name used to identify the fifth vacuum element
# % macro, DEVICE5, PV for the fifth element in the sequence
# % macro, DELAY5, ARM delay in seconds after the 'open disarmed' state (required for a fast valve, 30s recommended)
